    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d50-a1">

                <pb facs="0114" n="66" xml:id="pg66"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Montufar to Mr. Williamson.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Office of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1877-05-30"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 30,
                        1877</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In an opportune moment I had the honor to
                    receive your excellency’s estimable note dated the 24th instant. The President,
                    to whom I related its contents, was pleased to order that the postal convention
                    of 1862 should be literally complied with, that convention being still existing
                    between the United States and Guatemala. I informed the minister of public works
                    of this to-day.</p>
                <p>With sentiments of the most “distinguished esteem, I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>LORENZO MONTUFAR.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
